{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>For</b> — He mentioned the good things He did for Israel, that He brought them out with silver and gold and sustained them in the wilderness, until they came to the land; and all this was on account of His covenant that He began, as it says, 'He has remembered His covenant forever' — and He mentioned Abraham alone, for with him it was in truth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 105, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:34.521075903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}